CM_ "Mk60e5 DSC (M3, software 7846816A, unmodified) PT-CAN broadcast, trimmed for track logging. Checksums are left out; alive counters are included where they are useful.";
CM_ BO_ 196 "Steering angle relayed from the F-CAN steering sensor (0x0C9), 10 ms. Only meaningful with a steering sensor fitted. Bytes 5-6 are constant.";
CM_ SG_ 196 SteeringWheelAngle "Steering-wheel angle. Sign convention unverified.";
CM_ SG_ 196 SteeringWheelVelocity "Steering-wheel angular velocity, relayed from a sub-channel of the sensor frame and held between updates. Same raw scaling as the angle.";
CM_ SG_ 196 SteeringAngleStatus "Sensor status. 0 and 1 are passed through from the sensor; the meaning of 1 is a best guess.";
CM_ BO_ 206 "Wheel speeds, 20 ms. Raw per-wheel speed: no tyre-tolerance trim, not vref. Reads 0 below about 0.6 km/h. Negative when the wheel's direction is latched as reverse (direction updates below 55 km/h only).";
CM_ BO_ 414 "DSC/ABS status, 20 ms.";
CM_ SG_ 414 AbsActiveFront "A front wheel is in an ABS cycle.";
CM_ SG_ 414 TcsActive "Traction control (brake or engine) intervening.";
CM_ SG_ 414 YawTorqueActive "Yaw control is requesting an engine torque cut.";
CM_ SG_ 414 DscActive "DSC (yaw control) function active.";
CM_ SG_ 414 MsrActive "MSR (engine drag torque control) active.";
CM_ SG_ 414 AbsActiveRearOnly "A rear wheel is under ABS control and no front is (EBD-style rear control).";
CM_ SG_ 414 AbsStatus "2 = ABS switched off by a fault reaction, or ABS lamp on with ABS degraded.";
CM_ SG_ 414 DscStatus "First match wins, in order 2, 6, 3, 1, 4, else 0.";
CM_ SG_ 414 TorqueInterventionActive "1 = yaw-control torque request, or TCS active with a large torque cut (latched).";
CM_ SG_ 414 HillHoldCondition "1 = hill-start assist condition: driver pressure above threshold, car on a slope it can hold. Exact meaning (armed vs holding) unconfirmed.";
CM_ SG_ 414 BrakeSwitch "Brake-light switch. Reads 3 (invalid) unless 0x130 (terminal status) is received with byte 0 bits 0-1 = 1.";
CM_ SG_ 414 BrakeApplied "1 = brake switch on or any valid wheel pressure > 6 bar.";
CM_ SG_ 414 MasterCylPressure "Master-cylinder (driver) pressure, integer bar, clamped 0..254.";
CM_ BO_ 416 "Vehicle speed and body motion, 20 ms.";
CM_ SG_ 416 VehicleSpeed "Mean of the two FRONT wheel speeds (not vref, no tyre trim). Clamped to 300 km/h.";
CM_ SG_ 416 DriveDirection "From the front-wheel direction bits and the standstill detector.";
CM_ SG_ 416 AccelLongWheel "Longitudinal accel derived from the FRONT wheel accelerations, not the accelerometer. 0.0025 g/bit, clamped +/-1 g, low-passed (1st-order IIR, alpha 1/32), so it lags. Free of road slope, but wrong under front wheel slip/lock.";
CM_ SG_ 416 AccelLat "Lateral accel from the sensor cluster, offset-corrected. Sign unverified.";
CM_ SG_ 416 YawRate "Yaw rate from the sensor cluster, offset-corrected, clipped to +/-90 deg/s. Sign unverified.";
CM_ SG_ 416 AliveCounter "Steps every frame, 0..14 (15 skipped).";
CM_ BO_ 419 "Longitudinal accelerometer, 20 ms. No offset-corrected sensor ax is broadcast: corrected = AccelLongRaw - AccelLongOffset (make it a math channel).";
CM_ SG_ 419 AccelLongRaw "Raw accelerometer ax: unfiltered, no zero-offset correction, includes road gradient.";
CM_ SG_ 419 AccelLongOffset "Learned accelerometer zero offset (+/-0.238 g max), same scale as AccelLongRaw.";
CM_ SG_ 419 AccelLongRawStatus "Value 1 is never sent for the raw signal.";
CM_ SG_ 419 AccelLongOffsetStatus "1 = offset probably not learned yet.";
CM_ SG_ 419 AliveCounter "Steps every frame, 0..14 (15 skipped).";
CM_ BO_ 690 "Wheel brake pressures and brake pre-fill state, 20 ms.";
CM_ SG_ 690 BrakePressureFL "Measured/modelled wheel pressure, integer bar, clamped 0..254.";
CM_ SG_ 690 BrakePrefillState "Brake pre-fill on fast throttle lift. 0 = not coded or inhibited, 1 = armed, 2 = active.";
CM_ SG_ 690 DiscDryingState "Wet-disc drying (wiper-triggered). 0 = not coded or inhibited, 1 = armed, 2 = active.";
CM_ BO_ 884 "Learned per-wheel tyre tolerance trims, 1 s. Factor applied to the wheel's speed = 1 + TyreTrim/100. Trims are normalised so the slowest-turning wheel is 0; a negative trim means that wheel turns faster by that much. Clamped at -12.7 %.";
CM_ SG_ 884 TyreTrimStatus "0 after power-up; changes to 1 once the learner has adapted (typically after 1-2 km of driving).";
